  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe built-in Tencent Cloud TokenHub pay-as-you-go preset does not cover **Tencent Cloud International account + Guangzhou endpoint**. Using an API key issued from the Tencent Cloud International console with Magpie's **Pay as you go · China** region returns `401 Unauthorized` while fetching models.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a TokenHub API key in the **Tencent Cloud International** console for Guangzhou.\n2. In Magpie, add the **Tencent Cloud** provider, select **Pay as you go · China**, and enter the key.\n3. Click **Fetch models**.\n4. Magpie requests `https://tokenhub.tencentmaas.com/v1/models` and fails with:\n\n```text\n401 Unauthorized: The API Key does not exist or signature verification failed.\n```\n\n## Expected result\n\nThe International console's generated API example uses:\n\n```text\nPOST https://tokenhub.tencentcloudmaas.com/v1/chat/completions\nAuthorization: Bearer <key>\nmodel: glm-5.3\n```\n\nMagpie should support the corresponding OpenAI base URL `https://tokenhub.tencentcloudmaas.com/v1`.\n\n## Source-code reference\n\n`internal/provider/presets.go` defines:\n\n```go\n{ID: \"cn\", Name: \"Pay as you go · China\",\n    Chat: \"https://tokenhub.tencentmaas.com/v1\"},\n{ID: \"intl\", Name: \"Pay as you go · Global\",\n    Chat: \"https://tokenhub-intl.tencentmaas.com/v1\"},\n```\n\nNeither matches the `tokenhub.tencentcloudmaas.com` endpoint displayed in the Tencent Cloud International console.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nPlease add an **International account / Guangzhou** variant, or let users override base URLs on the built-in Tencent Cloud preset. Ideally distinguish **account site** (China/International) from **inference region** (Guangzhou/Singapore).\n\n## Notes\n\n- The expected API hostname is taken from the user's official Tencent Cloud International console example. I have not independently verified a successful request against that endpoint or the model-list route.\n- No credentials are included.\n",
