   "body": "The 401 is the account site, not the key: the Pay as you go · China region asks the China console's host tokenhub.tencentmaas.com, and an International console key does not exist there. The International console's own example (and its API usage page, https://intl.cloud.tencent.com/document/product/1300/78941) uses tokenhub.tencentcloudmaas.com, which no region of the preset served.\n\nThe branch adds a \"Pay as you go · Global · Guangzhou\" region (intl-gz) to the Tencent Cloud preset at https://tokenhub.tencentcloudmaas.com/v1 (chat completions and Responses under /v1, Anthropic messages at the bare host), with the tencent-tokenhub catalog, the International key page and docs, and the name translated in all four UI languages. The China and Singapore regions are unchanged; an entry imported at the Guangzhou endpoints lands on the new region, and magpie://import?preset=tencent-cloud&region=intl-gz names it. The Silicon Valley site (tokenhub-us.tencentcloudmaas.com) from the same page is not added, since nothing reported it — say if it should be.\n\nBranch, not a PR and no claim on the issue: [fix/3790-tencent-cloud-tokenhub-international-guangzhou](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/3790-tencent-cloud-tokenhub-international-guangzhou), commit 145879014bf5f780a0a9136b848d719f0bb418a5.\n\nRun: TestTencentCloudIntlGuangzhou fails without the change (intl-gz: <nil>) and passes with it; go build ./..., go vet ./internal/provider/, gofmt -l (clean), the whole internal/provider package (its only failure, TestCodexAppServersOnHome, fails the same way on clean upstream/main), and the GUI i18n-keys test's \"every word the window says has a key\". The endpoints are from Tencent's docs and the console example, not tried with a real International key.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
